# Frontend-to-Backend Migration Plan

This document outlines the strategy for shifting the application from a "Frontend-Direct-to-DB" (Appwrite SDK) approach to a "Backend-Oriented" approach.

## 🎯 Goal
Remove all direct Appwrite SDK calls from the frontend (Pages and Server Actions) and route all data operations through the Node.js backend API.

---

## 🛠️ Phase 1: Server Action Migration
We will migrate `frontend/lib/actions/student.actions.ts` and `frontend/lib/actions/auth.actions.ts` in four priority blocks.

### Block 1: Core Identity (High Priority)
*Goal: Ensure user session and profile management is secure and centralized.*
- [ ] `completeMenteeOnboarding` $\rightarrow$ `PUT /profiles/me`
- [ ] `updateProfileDetails` $\rightarrow$ `PATCH /profiles/me`
- [ ] `getMenteeProfile` $\rightarrow$ `GET /profiles/:id`
- [ ] `checkUserRole` $\rightarrow$ `GET /auth/role`

### Block 2: Interaction & Meetings (Highest Priority)
*Goal: Move the most frequent user interactions to the API.*
- [ ] `logMeeting` $\rightarrow$ `POST /meetings`
- [ ] `requestMeeting` $\rightarrow$ `POST /meetings/request`
- [ ] `updateMeetingStatus` $\rightarrow$ `PATCH /meetings/:id/status`
- [ ] `getMentorScheduledMeetings` $\rightarrow$ `GET /mentor/meetings`
- [ ] `getMeetingRequests` $\rightarrow$ `GET /mentor/requests`
- [ ] `updateScheduledMeetingAttendance` $\rightarrow$ `PATCH /meetings/:id/attendance`

### Block 3: Academic Tracking (Complexity Priority)
*Goal: Migrate file uploads and verification logic.*
- [ ] `uploadAcademicRecord` $\rightarrow$ `POST /academics` (Handle multipart/form-data)
- [ ] `uploadAchievement` $\rightarrow$ `POST /achievements`
- [ ] `updateAcademicStatus` $\rightarrow$ `PATCH /academics/:id/status`
- [ ] `updateAchievementStatus` $\rightarrow$ `PATCH /achievements/:id/status`
- [ ] `getAcademicRecordsForProfile` $\rightarrow$ `GET /profiles/:id/academics`
- [ ] `getAchievementRecordsForProfile` $\rightarrow$ `GET /profiles/:id/achievements`

### Block 4: Admin & Management (System Priority)
*Goal: Secure administrative operations.*
- [ ] `assignMentor` / `assignMentorToStudent` $\rightarrow$ `PATCH /admin/assign-mentor`
- [ ] `importMasterAdvisoryList` / `bulkImportStudents` $\rightarrow$ `POST /admin/import`
- [ ] `getSystemAnalytics` $\rightarrow$ `GET /admin/analytics`
- [ ] `deleteUserProfile` $\rightarrow$ `DELETE /admin/profiles/:id`
- [ ] `getGlobalSettings` / `updateGlobalSettings` $\rightarrow$ `GET/PATCH /admin/settings`

---

## 🎨 Phase 2: Frontend UI Data-Fetching Update
Even after server actions are migrated, many pages still instantiate the Appwrite SDK internally.

### 1. Component-Level Cleanup
- [ ] **Dashboard Overview Page** (`app/dashboard/[profileId]/page.tsx`): Remove `new Client()`, `new Databases()` and replace the massive `Promise.all` block with calls to migrated server actions.
- [ ] **Mentor Dashboard** (`app/mentor-dashboard/page.tsx`): Replace direct SDK fetching with centralized server actions.
- [ ] **Admin Dashboard**: Replace raw DB queries with API-backed actions.

### 2. API Client Optimization
- [ ] Implement a standardized Error Handling wrapper in `frontend/lib/api-client.ts` to parse backend errors consistently.
- [ ] Add TypeScript types for all API responses to ensure type safety between Backend $\rightarrow$ Action $\rightarrow$ UI.

### 3. State & Revalidation
- [ ] Audit all `revalidatePath` calls to ensure they trigger after backend mutations.
- [ ] Implement loading states (Skeletons) for the new API-based fetches to prevent UI flicker.

---

## 🧪 Phase 3: Verification & Testing
- [ ] **Auth Flow:** Test Sign-in $\rightarrow$ Profile $\rightarrow$ Dashboard sequence.
- [ ] **Meeting Flow:** Request Meeting (Student) $\rightarrow$ Approve (Mentor) $\rightarrow$ View (Both).
- [ ] **Academic Flow:** Upload PDF $\rightarrow$ Review (Mentor) $\rightarrow$ Verified status update.
- [ ] **Admin Flow:** CSV Import $\rightarrow$ Mentor Assignment $\rightarrow$ Analytics update.
